{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Let there please be no strife, etc.</b> The reason he said <b>between me and you</b> is to inform him that ultimately the strife will also be between the two of them. And although Lot might say that heaven forbid he would never contend with his master and prince, and the thing would never come to be, even so he would acknowledge the matter that already exists between his herdsmen and Abram's herdsmen — and that is his saying <b>and between my herdsmen</b>, etc. And his saying <b>for we are men, brothers</b> may be explained according to their words (Genesis Rabbah 41) that Lot's herdsmen used to send their flocks and shepherds into others' fields, with the claim that the land belongs to Abraham and to Lot his brother's son as inheritance. And this is the sense of the verse: ״אַל נָא תְהִי מְרִיבָה בֵּינִי״, etc. — by this statement, that we are men, brothers.\"" "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained along the lines of the verse (Psalms 50:20): ״תֵּשֵׁב בְּאָחִיךָ תְדַבֵּר בְּבֶן אִמְּךָ תִּתֶּן דֹּפִי״, which our earlier commentators explained in this manner: ״תֵּשֵׁב בְּאָחִיךָ בְּבֶן אִמְּךָ״ — it is you who speak, ״תִּתֶּן דֹּפִי.״ And this is what it says: ״כִּי אֲנָשִׁים אַחִים״ — meaning, when the strife comes about and they are brought before the judges of the land, who are the Canaanite and the Perizzite, mentioned by the verse immediately following, and when the judges of the land find both of them culpable, the blemish will also circle around to his brother, for both the biter and the bitten are held culpable for being brothers." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that since they are brothers, neither Lot nor his herdsmen conduct themselves with the honor due to Abraham, reckoning that there is no difference — whereas if Abraham and Lot were not close kin, they would have treated Abraham with honor on account of the exaltedness of his station, which Elohim had magnified."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:07.334301850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}